WEBVTT

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:26.750
<i>New days, it's the morning we begin. 
Let's give the world a kiss.</i>

00:00:27.710 --> 00:00:35.240
<i>Blowing in the wind, with a little 
courage and love in our pockets.</i>

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:44.090
<i>I wish: If only I had wings,</i>

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:53.690
<i>I could fly over the sadness, 
the past, and my doubts.</i>

00:00:53.690 --> 00:01:02.450
<i>Oh, yeah! There's nothing to lose. (Take 
whatever the brand new day brings.)</i>

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:07.290
<i>Take my way! I wanna catch a miracle...</i>

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:11.030
<i>in the palm of my hand!</i>

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:19.720
<i>We're off on a journey through the endless 
earth, the skies, and the future.</i>

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:32.140
<i>I know these newborn wings, oh! Are 
gonna gonna gonna shine someday!</i>

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:07.520
I'm tired!

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:08.930
Yeah, yeah...

00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:11.120
I'm tired!

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:12.020
Yes, yes...

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.560
I wanna have a hot meal

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:18.370
and climb into a nice, soft 
bed, and I want it right now!

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:19.870
Would you shut up?!

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:22.870
Is this the mouth that's spouting 
that self-centered garbage?! Is it?!

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:26.130
All we've done for ages is ride 
in the cart, camp outside,

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:28.000
and then do it all over again!

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.880
My butt is killing me, 
and I wanna take a bath!

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:34.700
Not until we've put some more distance 
between us and Manurhin town.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:35.600
You're mean!

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:49.390
"Overture of the Abandoned-Cat Princess"

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:51.270
Step down.

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:54.090
Oh, brother...

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:03.870
Is that girl Pacifica Cassul?

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:05.560
In the name of Mauser...

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:07.110
she must be destroyed!

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:09.870
You'd better stand back.

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:14.500
Barrier, obstruct them!

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:23.640
Son of a...

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:42.570
Aren't you going to fight?

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:45.800
Does that mean you're helpless?

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:49.120
So, all you can do is look on, huh?

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:57.670
Pacifica!

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:10.240
See you.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:19.790
Who was that guy?

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:21.990
Come on, let's go.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:35.330
You... You're the poison that 
will destroy the world...

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:38.380
Raquel...

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:46.890
There's a village up ahead.

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:49.580
We'll get some animal feed 
or something for you there.

00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:51.890
A fancy full-course meal! With dessert, too!

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:54.660
As you wish, Highness...

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:11.660
So, you're here.

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:17.250
Those assassins I sent earlier 
have apparently failed.

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:21.660
All you must do is guide the girl here.

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:25.560
Mauser watches over your actions.

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:28.680
I'm finished.

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:32.910
A fancy, full-course meal. With dessert.

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:34.180
Are you kidding me?

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:35.950
That was delicious.

00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:41.250
Too bad, I think there was a cute little 
café in the next town after this one...

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:44.750
Do you understand the 
situation you're in, kid?

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:47.310
We can't take routes that might 
attract any undue attention.

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:49.290
Not until we leave the kingdom of Leinwan.

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:50.400
What's two times two?

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:51.080
Four!

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:52.190
Two times three?

00:05:52.190 --> 00:05:53.200
Six!

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:54.480
Two times four?

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:55.040
Eight!

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:56.700
So, what's two times five?

00:05:56.700 --> 00:05:57.410
Ten!

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:58.870
Wow, that's amazing!

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:00.250
Just leave it to me!

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:02.000
I'm still having trouble...

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:04.960
If you use eggs or whatever, 
you'll pick it up right away.

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:05.870
Really?

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:09.190
Oh, right! Have you learned your 
lines for the play next week?

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:11.170
I have 'em down pat! Just leave it to me.

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:12.300
Wow... That's amazing!

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:16.660
Pacifica...

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:19.100
How about you, Shannon? Do <i>you </i>understand?!

00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:22.610
You're to address me as 
Your Highness, not "kid"!

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:24.790
Now hand over that dumpling!

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:27.360
Jerk! Some princess you are, you stray cat!

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:28.500
Whatever, just hand it over!

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:29.930
As if!

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:31.620
Pacifica?!

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:42.000
I'm in paradise...

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:48.170
We're sorry for damaging your rice plants.

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:49.850
Oh, that's all right.

00:06:49.850 --> 00:06:53.080
So, you know my daughter, eh?

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:55.290
Yes, sir. We met in Manurhin.

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:58.480
What a coincidence, running 
into Auntie Diana here!

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:02.040
Perhaps I'll help myself 
to a bath later, too.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:03.440
Now look here...

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:06.940
Oh, how adorable!

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:08.370
Is it yours, Diana?

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:09.440
Yes.

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:15.450
Oh, no!

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:16.950
I'm going to go check on the bath,

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:18.590
so could I trouble you to look 
after the baby for a while?

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:19.750
Of course.

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:22.040
Thank you.

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:28.330
Shannon, you made Pacifica 
cry all the time, too.

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:29.760
I suppose I did.

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:32.120
After all, she was a kid sister 
who came out of nowhere.

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:33.550
I didn't know what to make of her.

00:07:36.700 --> 00:07:40.560
And now that baby is fifteen...

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:45.060
Honestly, it's been forever 
since my last bath!

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:48.320
How many years has it been 
since we last saw you, Auntie?

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:49.570
About three?

00:07:50.050 --> 00:07:51.660
I suppose it has.

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:54.580
This is where I was born.

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:58.080
Wow, really? I have to admit, 
we were really surprised!

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:02.080
We never expected to run into 
someone from Manurhin here!

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:05.580
We'll find you some dinner later.

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:08.590
Perhaps one of those egg dishes 
you're so fond of, Pacifica.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:10.250
Eggs?!

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:13.090
But first, could you help me with something?

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:16.830
Is your father well?

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:18.150
Well, he...

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:21.040
Our dad died just a little while ago.

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:22.100
Oh, he did?

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:25.580
Dad really appreciated you, Auntie.

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:29.110
I mean, after Mom died, he turned 
to you for everything, remember?

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:33.660
You'd even sit up with me all 
night when I had a fever.

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:36.730
And today, I come out of 
nowhere and use your bath...

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:40.000
A church?

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:43.370
I always get them to 
share their eggs with me.

00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:46.880
Would you help me carry them?

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:52.520
Auntie Diana?

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:53.990
She's not here?

00:08:54.700 --> 00:08:56.110
Neither is Pacifica.

00:08:57.520 --> 00:08:59.570
You don't suppose that Auntie...

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:02.850
In any case, let's look for them.

00:09:10.630 --> 00:09:13.550
Oh, you're that boy from earlier!

00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:19.430
Um, you haven't seen that 
girl around, have you?

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:20.830
Couldn't say.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:24.830
Um...

00:09:26.750 --> 00:09:30.340
The soy-sauce dumplings here are delicious!

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:55.610
This is the girl?

00:09:56.700 --> 00:10:01.720
The girl who it is said will usher in the 
world's destruction when she turns sixteen.

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:02.990
The Scrapped Princess.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:06.370
No way!

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:09.370
Well done. You may go now.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:12.590
Wha...? Auntie!

00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:15.080
Why?

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:18.580
I can't believe that you're 
the Scrapped Princess...

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:21.200
What I'm doing is for the 
good of the kingdom...

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:23.390
For the good of Mauser!

00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:25.680
You only have yourself to blame!

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:32.480
How foolish.

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:35.560
There is no need to feel 
shame over a good deed.

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:40.990
There is not a single place in 
this world that will take you in.

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:43.730
For you are the Scrapped Princess, 
whom Saint Grendel determined

00:10:43.730 --> 00:10:47.870
in his revelation to be the great 
evil that will destroy the world.

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:50.620
In the name of Mauser,

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:53.100
I shall purge the Scrapped Princess.

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:14.490
Thunder, rumble in the heavens,

00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:16.480
brandish your whip of light,

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:19.880
and display to us your wrath!

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:32.420
The father who raised you 
gave his life to protect you.

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:34.790
As long as you still live,

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:39.190
there will be more and more 
people who will flock to Mauser.

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:43.790
Your very existence is a sin.

00:11:43.790 --> 00:11:46.950
You should never have been born.

00:11:46.950 --> 00:11:50.430
For you were destined to 
be cast away immediately.

00:12:07.870 --> 00:12:12.290
My apologies, but I'm going to 
have to put you out of commission.

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:13.870
What in the...

00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:15.750
Um, Raquel...

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:16.790
Thunder,

00:12:17.150 --> 00:12:19.380
rumble in the heavens and brandish...

00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:19.380
People of the flames, dance!

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:25.500
Thunder,

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:28.310
rumble in the heavens and brandish...

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:28.310
People of the flames, dance!

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.640
Thunder...

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.640
People of the flames, dance!

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:43.150
A-Are you kidding me?!

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:47.840
You can't possibly call up any magic 
with a short incantation like that!

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:52.290
Do you mean to defy Mauser?!

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:53.990
Such insolence!

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:58.670
My deepest apologies.

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:00.910
I will in good faith confront 
you to the best of my abilities.

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:03.860
Class one tactical grade 
military offensive spell...

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:06.680
Come forth, Thor!

00:13:19.410 --> 00:13:20.910
Don't you think that was a bit much?!

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:22.830
But he said...

00:13:22.830 --> 00:13:24.190
Oh, it's Shannon.

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:26.640
What do you mean, "Oh"?!

00:13:28.420 --> 00:13:34.200
Now we've as good as told our pursuers 
that we stopped in this village...

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:35.620
I couldn't help it!

00:13:35.620 --> 00:13:37.040
Oh, brother...

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:38.400
Listen, Pacifica!

00:13:38.400 --> 00:13:40.210
I don't want you messing around 
on your own ever again!

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:42.950
Don't wander off with strangers!

00:13:43.540 --> 00:13:45.830
But she wasn't a stranger...

00:13:58.250 --> 00:13:59.950
Help me...

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:03.610
For one of the church's elite Attenuators, 
you're not all that impressive.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:06.660
I come all this way, and this is what I find?

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:09.680
I'll be the one who slays 
the Scrapped Princess.

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:15.830
Don't use any magic, understand?

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:18.160
Why not? It's so convenient...

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:21.290
One time out of three, it's 
a total failure, that's why!

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:24.450
Charbroiled barbecue. Exploding chicken.

00:14:24.450 --> 00:14:25.700
Need I go on?

00:14:25.700 --> 00:14:28.550
She's right! I'm sick of lousy food!

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:31.570
You're in no position to talk, kid!

00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:33.170
I'm starving...

00:14:33.170 --> 00:14:34.280
Don't eat that!

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:36.560
Ack... It's half-raw.

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:39.570
When you want something done fast, 
magic is the way to go, all right...

00:14:39.570 --> 00:14:40.560
Don't do it!

00:14:40.890 --> 00:14:42.200
Why not?

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:45.160
Look, just leave it alone!

00:15:01.680 --> 00:15:02.950
What do you want?

00:15:05.350 --> 00:15:09.080
Shannon, you're like an old 
man, hunched over like that.

00:15:09.080 --> 00:15:11.550
You got out of bed to pick a fight with me?

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:16.860
These nights are getting colder and colder!

00:15:16.860 --> 00:15:18.980
And you sound like an old lady, Pacifica.

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:23.980
That name, "Pacifica"...

00:15:24.350 --> 00:15:25.790
Who gave it to me?

00:15:25.790 --> 00:15:26.980
What do you mean?

00:15:27.550 --> 00:15:29.990
Mom and Dad, who else?

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:36.990
So my real mom and dad 
never gave me a name...

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:42.880
I wish I could have lived 
in that village forever...

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:46.980
With Dad, and Mom, and you, and Raquel...

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:49.330
I'd go to school, and we'd 
talk about pointless stuff...

00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:51.660
And I'd get chewed out for my bad grades...

00:15:51.660 --> 00:15:54.970
And I'd get mad and ask if I could 
get a raise in my allowance...

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:56.430
And I'd also...

00:15:57.580 --> 00:15:58.690
Pacifica...

00:15:59.490 --> 00:16:02.020
Didn't you want that, too, Shannon?

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:06.400
You know, take over from Dad 
and run the weapons store,

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:07.500
and live a normal...

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:09.530
I'll be able to do that again someday.

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:11.650
No you can't!

00:16:11.650 --> 00:16:13.300
Not as long as I'm around.

00:16:14.860 --> 00:16:18.250
I guess I really am trash, aren't I?

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:26.210
If I died, maybe all this would be over...

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:27.510
Right?

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:42.980
I'm gonna have Raquel take the next watch.

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:56.650
Answer my question!

00:16:58.440 --> 00:17:00.540
That's a tough one.

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:03.870
If...

00:17:06.030 --> 00:17:07.080
If it comes to it...

00:17:13.580 --> 00:17:15.700
You're that guy from this morning...

00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:16.630
Please die.

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:22.630
Get inside the cart!

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:26.670
Who are you?

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:28.670
Royal Forces, Fifth Special Ops Unit.

00:17:28.670 --> 00:17:30.160
The "Obstinate Arrows."

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:33.290
Christopher Armalite, Spec 
Ops Combat Techniques.

00:17:33.290 --> 00:17:34.490
You can call me Chris.

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:54.480
Now I get it.

00:17:54.480 --> 00:17:57.800
This certainly explains why you were able to 
protect the Scrapped Princess all this time.

00:17:58.370 --> 00:17:59.800
Oh, my!

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:03.310
Did you try their dumplings?

00:18:06.450 --> 00:18:10.510
Well, I guess it might be a bit 
difficult to beat both of you.

00:18:10.510 --> 00:18:12.090
I know it's rude to attack and run,

00:18:12.090 --> 00:18:13.800
but let's finish this another time.

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:18.630
Oh, that reminds me. One more thing.

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:20.820
Why are you two protecting that girl?

00:18:22.210 --> 00:18:24.470
You know about that revelation, right?

00:18:25.280 --> 00:18:27.700
That girl is an abomination 
who is going to bring down

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:29.830
disaster on the world when she turns sixteen.

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:32.840
No one will care if she dies.

00:18:33.260 --> 00:18:35.380
On the contrary, a great 
many people will celebrate.

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:38.870
What's the point of protecting a girl like...

00:18:40.490 --> 00:18:42.050
Did I make you mad?

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:43.950
Surely you're used to hearing that by now.

00:18:43.950 --> 00:18:48.350
That girl's name was given to 
her by our old man and our mom.

00:18:49.080 --> 00:18:53.100
They named her that in the hope 
that everyone would love her.

00:18:54.870 --> 00:18:58.360
I'm going to keep her safe.

00:18:59.170 --> 00:19:01.080
Right up until the last instant,

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:04.370
when I find out for sure if she really is 
the poison that will destroy the world.

00:19:17.450 --> 00:19:20.290
That guy is worlds apart from 
the people we've faced so far.

00:19:20.290 --> 00:19:21.520
Yes...

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:24.100
It looks like someone amazing has turned up.

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:32.670
Big brother...

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:36.650
If I...

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:41.990
If it turns out that I really 
am gonna destroy the world...

00:19:43.510 --> 00:19:48.790
If that happens, I want you to kill me, okay?

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:03.760
Aw, c'mon, how much farther 
to the next village?

00:20:04.160 --> 00:20:05.470
I don't know.

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:07.390
Of course you know!

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:10.770
You're always so vague and 
noncommittal, Shannon!

00:20:11.200 --> 00:20:14.480
Girls fundamentally hate guys like that!

00:20:14.480 --> 00:20:17.180
Yeah, sure. You don't say.

00:20:30.040 --> 00:20:31.320
Big brother?

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:34.160
The thing is...

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:39.530
I love you a lot.

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:45.130
Yeah, I know.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:54.140
Ow! Cut it out!

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:56.270
How about blushing a little 
or acting happy about it?!

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:58.390
I swear, you're so unendearing!

00:20:58.390 --> 00:21:00.820
What's your problem, anyway?! What's 
with that old geezer reaction?!

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:01.840
Well, excuse me!

00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:03.490
I can't stand that!

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:21.730
<i>A blessing of rain falls quietly. (Falls.)</i>

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:27.050
<i>Droplets of my love, 
which fall for someone...</i>

00:21:27.050 --> 00:21:34.230
<i>who is still waiting in a land far away.</i>

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:40.020
<i>The morning wind blows, caressing 
my cheek. (What was that...)</i>

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:45.150
<i>Did you feel something, feel something 
just now? (...on my cheek?)</i>

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:48.320
<i>It goes up to the one and only sky... 
(More certain than anything.)</i>

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:53.370
<i>a sky which has a fixed, certain meaning.</i>

00:21:53.370 --> 00:21:59.920
<i>I come to a stop in the shadow 
of clouds that chase after me.</i>

00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:03.380
<i>This journey of the heart 
that I wish to gaze upon...</i>

00:22:03.380 --> 00:22:06.590
<i>goes on forever and goes on forever.</i>

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:13.220
<i>One day I will chance upon the 
voice I've not heard in so long.</i>

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:15.180
<i>Alainn la-li-la.</i>

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:19.900
<i>At last the ship sets sail, sets 
sail. (The ship glides on forever...)</i>

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:25.190
<i>Yes, believe in this wide world... 
(...to the edge of seas unknown.)</i>

00:22:25.190 --> 00:22:28.530
<i>and go off into the distance.</i>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:32.630
<i>And onwards into the future.</i>

00:22:33.490 --> 00:22:46.510
"Next Time"

00:22:34.140 --> 00:22:36.750
The Cassuls are attacked by bandits.

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:40.580
A boy who happens to be passing by steps 
in to intervene, trying to rescue them.

00:22:40.580 --> 00:22:44.000
What's more, he decides to tag along 
even though they tell him not to.

00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:45.710
This could cause problems...

00:22:45.710 --> 00:22:47.720
Next time on <i>Scrapped Princess</i>,

00:22:47.720 --> 00:22:49.380
"March of the Half-Baked Knight."

00:22:49.380 --> 00:22:50.510
Please tune in!
